A||N||7||87ECO5||4 to 6 engine conversion running hot - are 2.5 and 2.8 radiators interchangeable?||||5||
Z||000000||87ECO5||08-13-2001||03:54 PM||||Back in April, I had my '87 coupe converted from a 2.5 to a remanufactured 3.4 V6.  I've been noticing over the last several weeks that the temp gauge climbs easily and rapidly to around 230, at which point the aux. fan kicks on and brings things back down to a tick or two below 220.  Unfortunately, the temp cycles like this until I flip on the A/C which keeps the temp down but also brings down my power output and fuel economy.<P>I've had several suggestions as to how to correct this:<P>1) replace the single-core 4-cylinder radiator with a dual-core unit from a V6 car.<BR>2) install a manual fan switch that will allow me to manually turn on the aux. fan without the need for the A/C.<BR>3) install a low-temp fan switch from Rodney Dickman.<BR>4) install a lower degree thermostat (which I did - I was running a 195 degree, I put in a 180 last night ... it didn't help).<P>Someone also suggested simply flushing and filling the system, which I'm going to do first (even though it was just done in April when the conversion was performed).  My guess is that maybe the system has air in it.<P>The 4-cylinder radiator stayed in the car after the conversion and it's the original so I'm sure it's overdue to be replaced.  My questions are:<P>1) is a V6 radiator "plug and play"?  Can I swap in a V6 unit without having to change out hoses or anything?<BR>2) do you think the reason for the "high" temps is due to the use of a 4-cylinder unit?||||reg||5
Z||000001||turbo86se||08-14-2001||12:25 AM||||I wish I could help you more, but I have had no problems with my stock 4-cyl radiator with the V6 installed in my 88 coupe. <BR>Take care!||||reg||5
Z||000002||Archie||08-14-2001||12:44 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 87ECO5:<BR><B><BR>1) is a V6 radiator "plug and play"?  Can I swap in a V6 unit without having to change out hoses or anything?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes it is.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000003||Primaris||08-14-2001||12:47 AM||||The thermostat sets the low temp of the engine and the fan switch sets the high.  So replacing the fan switch to a lower one should solve your problem.<P>------------------<BR>Signatures are a waste of bandwidth!||||reg||1
Z||000004||rockcrawl||08-14-2001||07:20 AM||||This picture shows two four cyl radiators, the one on the left has the heavy duty cool option and is the same thickness as a V6 rad. <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/DCP01288.jpg"> <BR>||||reg||7
Z||000005||isthiswhereiputausername?||08-14-2001||12:02 PM||||<BR>i have been running a v6 in my 84 since 1995,  And it dont heat up anymore then my 4 did.   You may want to hook up an extra switch to turn your fan on if your stuck in traffic, etc..<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fierokid87||08-14-2001||01:06 PM||||Well Im not sure.  but the replacement readiators from the Fierostore are all the same for both engines.  <P>Scott<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="BLOODY"> Fierokid's  Web site<BR>http://www.angelfire.com/sports/sfiero<P>AIM: Fierokid87<BR>ICQ: Fierokid</FONT><P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sfiero.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||rockcrawl||08-14-2001||05:19 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>but the replacement readiators from the Fierostore are all the same for both engines<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Yes I have noticed that the aftermarket replacements usually only come in one size. But the OEM radiators had many variations. Besides the thickness, the # of fins per inch also varies. According to the pros at Griffin Radiator, the fin count is adjusted for the volume and velocity of airflow, so I assume that maybe GM had different ones depending on which front fascia is on the car. Someone with a 22P manual should be able to tell. On a quick search, I just turned up 7 different AC Delco #s for Fiero radiators. There's more to it than just V6 or L4. Not that it matters, just some info I wanted to share.||||reg||1
